From 3b12eee7d6c9b308212bb06abc548b726fbb1e83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:04:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Name Google's help centre as Google's

The connection-help page sends a reader to
support.google.com/chrome/answer/6098869 to finish removing software that
intercepts connections. The rename in 0044 caught the anchor text and left the
link, so it offered a Bare help centre that does not exist and never did.

The rule the rename set out is that Google products keep their names, and this
is a page in Google's help centre, so it says so. The URL is unchanged: there is
nowhere else for it to point.
---
 components/security_interstitials_strings.grdp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/security_interstitials_strings.grdp b/components/security_interstitials_strings.grdp
index 75a95469184..8c5be5f81ef 100644
--- a/components/security_interstitials_strings.grdp
+++ b/components/security_interstitials_strings.grdp
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@
       &lt;li&gt;Under &lt;strong&gt;Startup type&lt;/strong&gt;, select &lt;strong&gt;Disabled&lt;/strong&gt;
       &lt;li&gt;Under &lt;strong&gt;Service status&lt;/strong&gt;, click &lt;strong&gt;Stop&lt;/strong&gt;
       &lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;Apply&lt;/strong&gt;, then click &lt;strong&gt;OK&lt;/strong&gt;
-      &lt;li&gt;Visit the &lt;a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/6098869"&gt;Bare help center&lt;/a&gt; to learn how to permanently remove the software from your computer
+      &lt;li&gt;Visit the &lt;a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/6098869"&gt;Chrome help center&lt;/a&gt; to learn how to permanently remove the software from your computer
       &lt;/ol&gt;
     </message>
   </if>
